s 1:5 (in metaphor), bow Hosea 1:5 ; Jer 49:35 , and sword Hosea 2:20 ( מִןהָֿאָרֶץ ), bone of lamb Exod 12:46 ; Num 9:12 (P), and (in metaphor) Prov 25:15 , compare שָׁבוּר i.e. fractured of limb Lev 22:22 (H), yoke Jer 28:10 , 12 , 13 , and, in metaphor, of deliverance ( ׳י subject) 28:2 ; 28:4 ; 28:11 ; 38:8 (with מֵעַל ), +4 t., of rebellion 2:20 ; 5:5 , so staff Isa 14:5 5 t., reed 42:3 , arm of Pharaoh Ezek 30:21-22 , 24 compare Psa 10:15 ; trees (subject thunder) 29:5 ; break in, down , door Gen 19:9 (J); rend violently (of lion), man 1Kin 13:26 , ass 13:28 ; wreck Tyre (as ship) Ezek 27:26 ; figurative break pride Lev 26:19 (H); crush (figurative) Isa 14:25 (compare Jer 48:28 above), Lam 1:15 ; Dan 11:26 ; שׁ שִׁבָּרוֺן ׳מִשְׁנֶה Jer 17:18 ; break, rupture , heart (figurative) Psa 69:21 + Ezek 6:9 (see Niph`al near the end ), לֵב שְׁבוּרֵי Psa 147:3 ; חֻקִּי עָלָיו וָאֶשְׁבֹּר Job 38:10 broke for it my boundary , of sea, reference to abrupt ending of mainland; = quench thirst ( frangere sitim ) Psa 104:11 . Niph`al 57 Perfect 3masculine singular נִשְׁבַּר Exod 22:9 +, etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִשָּׁבֵר Lev 6:21 +, 3 feminine singular וְתִשָּׁ֫בֶר Eccl 12:6 , 2 masculine singular תִּשָּׁבֵר Ezek 29:7 , שַבר - 32:28 , etc.; Infinitive construct הִשָּׁבֵר Jonah 1:4 Participle נִשְׁבָּר Psa 51:19 , feminine singular נִשְׁבָּרָה 51:19 , נִשְׁבֶּ֫רֵת Ezek 27:34 +, etc.; — be broken , of neck 1Sam 4:18 , bones Psa 34:21 , gate-bars Jer 51:30 , rod (in figurative) Isa 14:21 ; Jer 48:17 , idols Ezek 6:4 , 6 , horn Dan 8:8 , compare 8:22 , arm Job 31:22 ( מִקָּנָה ), and (in metaphor) Jer 48:25 ; Job 38:15 ; Psa 37:17 , compare Ezek 30:22 , bough 31:12 ; Isa 27:11 , compare (figurative) of wickedness, like a tree Job 24:20 , other things Psa 37:15 ; Jer 50:23 ; Ezek 29:7 ; Psa 124:7 ; cisterns Jer 2:13 ( id. ), pottery Lev 6:21 ; 15:12 (P), Eccl 12:6 (in figurative); = be maimed, crippled (have limb broken), of animal Exod 22:9 ; 22:13 (E), and (figurative) Ezek 34:4